        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Aura of Annihilation"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(aura, necromancy, occult)\n\n60 feet, 45. A creature entering or starting its turn in the aura that fails at a Fortitude save becomes doomed 1 and drained 1. If the target was already doomed or drained, the values of these conditions increase by 1, to a maximum of doomed 3 and drained 3. A creature that dies while doomed 3 and drained 3 in this way disintegrates into black sand."
            },
            "id": "fe55e3ce-7039-4c3c-91e6-ba53d8d8ac36",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-19T22:58:57.944374"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Unkillable"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(necromancy, occult)\n\nUnlike most undead, Iffdahsil isn't destroyed at 0 HP. Iffdahsil's fast healing continues to function normally, though on any round it begins its turn at 0 HP, it is enfeebled 4 and slowed 1 until the start of its next turn. While Iffdahsil is at 0 HP, it can be killed permanently only by simultaneously exposing it to direct sunlight (or a 10th-level sunburst spell) and casting a miracle or wish spell (or similar magic) directed at destroying it."
            },
            "id": "3e203580-f2c5-453f-8f1b-67fa05d1974f",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-19T22:58:57.944374"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Eat Away"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "A creature that begins its turn inside Iffdahsil takes 10d6 negative damage. Iffdahsil gains temporary HP for 1 minute equal to half the damage dealt."
            },
